            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-  Receptacles

-  All windows 

-  All exterior doors

-  Bathrooms fans

- Kitchen fan

- Floor heating register



During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <HeatingSystem>Have you already thought about having a heat pump? This type of heating system can use up to 3 times less energy than a typical baseboard and needs electricity to operate. However, this kind of system cant operate on temperature below -25 degrees Celsius, it then requires a secondary system to maintain the heat. In this case, the furnace can ensure the heat and the ducting system can be used by the heat pump to supply heat in the entire building. You might be eligible to participate in the Heat Pumps pilot project, please follow the link below for more information;

https://yukon.ca/en/news/expanded-rebates-renewable-home-heating-now-available



</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
